Language name: Aether
RegEx for Number literals, Letter literals, and Identifiers:
Numbers: "^\\d+$" 
Letter: "^[a-zA-Z]$" (handles the part of decimals in a seperate function)
Identifiers: "^[a-zA-Z_][a-zA-Z0-9_]*$"

Running the scanner: If you run the scanner file without any arguments or files you will be placed 
in the AetherTest Mode where you are free to type statements that the scanner reads and reports
tokens back from. If you enter a file as an argument while running the scanner file then it will read the file 
and report the tokens in the source code from the file until the end of the file. If you have more than 1 file 
it will report that there were too many arguments and exit the program. 

My test cases in the test file I used some actual statements you may see in an actual source code file
and also alot of different characters and Identifiers that may show up as well. The scanner reported
errors for certain unhandled characters such as the @ symbol that would be considered an edge case I can handle 
by implementing it as a character for a string. 

